course: dictionary
lesson: 7279
title: One word, many meanings: ping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «ping» has several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The microwave pings when the food is ready.» Here a ping is a short, high ringing sound, like a bell.
explain: «I'll ping you an email.» Here ping is a verb meaning to send someone a quick message. Ask yourself what would fit: the word email is the clue, so ping must mean send.
explain: In games and computers, ping is a number. «Ping is a number showing how long data takes to travel; lower ping means less lag.» Lag is a delay, so a low ping means a fast connection.
fact: A ping can be a noun («a ping») or a verb («to ping»).
fact: As a noun, a ping is a short, high, ringing sound, like a bell or a phone alert.
fact: Informally, to ping someone is to send them a quick message.
fact: In computing, a ping is a test signal sent to check whether a computer can be reached and how fast it answers.
fact: «Sonar sends a ping and times the echo; sound travels about four times faster in water than in air.»
exercise: «The microwave pings when the food is ready.» What does pings mean here? | *A short, high ringing sound | To swim fast across a pool | A lot of heavy rain
exercise: Mia says, «I'll ping you later.» What does ping mean? | To fall asleep quickly | *To send someone a quick message | To hit a ball over a net
exercise: «Lower ping means less lag in an online game.» What does ping measure? | How many games you have won | How loud your headset is | *How long data takes to travel and come back | How old your computer is
test: «Sonar sends a ping and times the echo.» What does sonar time? | *The echo | The fish in the sea | The ping sound
test: Jack's game is lagging, so he checks his ping. Why does a high ping cause lag? | His screen is too bright | Games are always slow at night | *Messages take longer to reach the server
exam: «Connor's game lagged badly, because his ping was very high.» What does ping mean here? | A short ringing sound | To send a quick message | *A number showing how long data takes to travel
